note SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-only
note goal2en: R45 goal line G -> one fixed-template English review sentence
note that states every operand. G is validated by the contract lane's
note ocsetgl (msg.om); an invalid G prints `G2E_INVALID goal <reason>` and
note returns 31. Needs otio.om, vocab.om, msg.om, otmsg.om before it and
note otfrag.om after it. Templates are documented in TRANSLATOR.md.
text otfr "Goal for review: one matmul_u32 job multiplying a | by | matrix by a | matrix with seed |.\n|Goal for review: two matmul_u32 jobs, each multiplying a | matrix, with seeds | and | in that order.\n|G2E_INVALID goal |usage: goal2en < goal\n"

note "a {m} by {k} matrix by a {k} by {n}" after fragment 0 or 5.
fn otgdims m ulong k ulong n ulong to void
otpdec m
otpfr 1
otpdec k
otpfr 2
otpdec k
otpfr 1
otpdec n
end

note goal2en on otin[0..n): fills otob, returns 0 or 31.
fn otgoalen n ulong to int
if gt n 0
if eq get otin sub n 1 10
n = sub n 1
end
end
ok = otcopy 0 n
if not ok
otpfr 9
otprs neg long 10
otpb 10
ret 31
end
v = ocsetgl n
if lt v 0
otpfr 9
otprs v
otpb 10
ret 31
end
m = get ocgv 1
k = get ocgv 2
nn = get ocgv 3
if eq get ocgv 0 7
otpfr 5
otgdims m k nn
otpfr 6
otpdec get ocgv 4
otpfr 7
otpdec get ocgv 5
otpfr 8
ret 0
end
otpfr 0
otgdims m k nn
otpfr 3
otpdec get ocgv 4
otpfr 4
ret 0
end
